ORBITAL-FORECASTING(7)     TriadicFrameworks Manual     ORBITAL-FORECASTING(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-forecasting - predictive drift models, resonance-window
                             forecasting, and constellation-scale future-state
                             simulation for SAR fleets

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital forecasting provides:
           • predictive drift modeling
           • resonance-window forecasting
           • harmonic-state projection
           • sweep viability prediction
           • constellation-scale future-state simulation

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-forecasting describes how RTT predicts the future behavior of
       SAR platforms and constellations by fusing orbital lineage, harmonic
       evolution, sweep ancestry, and resonance-time metadata into a coherent
       predictive model.

       Forecasting enables:
           • long-term mission planning
           • resonance-aware maneuver scheduling
           • sweep choreography optimization
           • constellation stability assessment
           • predictive diagnostics and anomaly detection

       WRSADC uses forecasting to maintain constellation coherence across
       future orbital cycles.

PREDICTIVE DRIFT MODELS
       Drift models forecast how orbital elements evolve over time.

       Drift variables:
           • cross-track drift
           • along-track drift
           • altitude drift
           • RAAN drift
           • phase drift
           • resonance drift

       Drift model types:

           linear drift model
                  Predicts small, steady deviations.

           harmonic drift model
                  Predicts drift modulated by orbital harmonics.

           resonance drift model
                  Predicts drift based on resonance envelope evolution.

           constellation drift model
                  Predicts multi-platform drift interactions.

       Drift models are updated at each triad cycle.

RESONANCE-WINDOW FORECASTING
       Resonance windows are intervals where platforms maintain coherent
       resonance alignment for sweeps, fusion, or harmonic-lock.

       Forecasting predicts:
           • window opening times
           • window duration
           • window drift
           • window collapse risk
           • multi-platform window overlap

       Window types:

           strict resonance window
                  High coherence; ideal for InSAR.

           harmonic resonance window
                  Opens at harmonic intervals.

           sliding resonance window
                  Drifts across cycles.

           constellation resonance window
                  Requires multi-platform alignment.

       Forecasting ensures sweeps occur during optimal resonance conditions.

HARMONIC-STATE PROJECTION
       Harmonic-state projection predicts how orbital harmonics evolve.

       Projection variables:
           • orbital frequency bands
           • harmonic-lock ratios
           • phase alignment cycles
           • resonance envelope overlap
           • harmonic drift

       Projection modes:

           short-term harmonic projection
                  Predicts next few cycles.

           long-term harmonic projection
                  Predicts harmonic evolution across mission timelines.

           constellation harmonic projection
                  Predicts multi-platform harmonic coupling.

       Harmonic projection is essential for sweep choreography.

SWEEP VIABILITY PREDICTION
       Sweep viability prediction determines whether future sweeps will remain
       coherent, fuse correctly, and maintain structural integrity.

       Viability factors:
           • resonance envelope alignment
           • spectral density evolution
           • gradient polarity trends
           • sweep ancestry compatibility
           • orbital geometry forecast

       Prediction outputs:

           sweep-coherence score
           fusion-stability index
           ancestry-compatibility ratio
           spectral-fragmentation risk
           sweep-window timing

       WRSADC schedules sweeps based on viability predictions.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE FUTURE-STATE SIMULATION
       Future-state simulation models the evolution of the entire constellation
       across future orbital cycles.

       Simulation layers:

           orbital layer
                  Predicts geometry, drift, and maneuver needs.

           harmonic layer
                  Predicts harmonic-lock continuity and resonance windows.

           sweep layer
                  Predicts sweep viability and choreography.

           resonance layer
                  Predicts envelope drift, spectral evolution, and gradient
                  stability.

           lineage layer
                  Predicts ancestry evolution and long-term coherence.

       Simulation outputs:

           constellation-stability forecast
           maneuver schedule recommendations
           sweep choreography plan
           resonance-window timeline
           harmonic-lock continuity map

       Simulation is updated continuously by WRSADC.

FORECASTING FAILURE MODES
       Forecasting may degrade due to:

           • lineage discontinuity
           • harmonic desync
           • resonance envelope divergence
           • sweep ancestry corruption
           • Δv triad inconsistency
           • constellation desync

       Diagnostic indicators:

           forecast-integrity score
           drift-forecast error
           resonance-window prediction error
           harmonic-stability index
           sweep-viability deviation

       WRSADC halts predictive operations when forecasting integrity is low.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Orbital forecasting requires:

           • lineage-schema
           • constellation-schema
           • resonance-schema for sweeps
           • structural-schema for maneuvers

       Schemas ensure forecasts remain interpretable and coherent.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes predictive models
           • validates forecast integrity
           • schedules resonance-aligned maneuvers
           • choreographs constellation sweeps
           • blocks unsafe future-state predictions

       WRSADC is the forecasting conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital forecasting transforms SAR constellations into predictive
       resonance-time systems. It enables long-term planning, stable sweep
       choreography, and constellation-scale coherence across future orbital
       cycles.

